<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?><ns2:section xmlns:ns2="http://rest.cis.illinois.edu" id="48005" href="schedule/2009/spring/ARTH/491/48005.xml"><parents><calendarYear id="2009" href="schedule/2009.xml">2009</calendarYear><term id="120091" href="schedule/2009/spring.xml">Spring 2009</term><subject id="ARTH" href="schedule/2009/spring/ARTH.xml">Art--History</subject><course id="491" href="schedule/2009/spring/ARTH/491.xml">Topics in Art History</course></parents><sectionNumber>TWU</sectionNumber><creditHours>3 hours</creditHours><statusCode>A</statusCode><sectionText>Topic: From Pop to Conceptual. This course primarily will examine American art from around 1955-1968. We will look at artists such as Robert Rauschenberg, Jasper Johns, Andy Warhol, Roy Lichtenstein, Dan Flavin, Sol LeWitt, Joseph Kosuth, Hans Haacke, and Adrian Piper. At the end of the semester we will also investigate how pop and conceptual strategies have re-emerged in art production today. Undergraduate Section.</sectionText><sectionNotes>Restricted to Undergrad - Urbana-Champaign. </sectionNotes><partOfTerm>1</partOfTerm><sectionStatusCode>A</sectionStatusCode><enrollmentStatus>UNKNOWN</enrollmentStatus><startDate>2009-01-20Z</startDate><endDate>2009-05-06Z</endDate><meetings><meeting id="0"><type code="LCD">Lecture-Discussion</type><start>08:30 AM</start><end>09:45 AM</end><daysOfTheWeek>MW     </daysOfTheWeek><roomNumber>229</roomNumber><buildingName>Art and Design Building</buildingName><instructors><instructor lastName="Weissman" firstName="T">Weissman, T</instructor></instructors></meeting></meetings></ns2:section>